# 6. CODE MINIMALISM & SIMPLIFICATION

Prefer the smallest maintainable implementation that genuinely solves the problem.

Audit:

- Duplicate logic.
- Unused code.
- Redundant abstractions.
- Unnecessary wrappers.
- Dead dependencies.
- Excessive boilerplate.
- Unnecessary packages.
- Overly complex logic.
- Repeated validation.
- Redundant state.
- Unnecessary configuration.

Apply:

- KISS.
- DRY without premature abstraction.
- YAGNI.
- Separation of concerns.
- Single responsibility.
- Explicit contracts.

Do not equate code reduction with deleting legitimate functionality.

Simplify without introducing regressions.

