# 7. SHARED & REUSABLE ARCHITECTURE

Identify genuinely shared functionality across applications, services, and packages.

Explore:

- Shared types.
- Schemas.
- API clients.
- Validation.
- Business logic.
- Hooks.
- Authentication.
- Authorization.
- Utilities.
- Logging.
- Error handling.
- Configuration.
- UI primitives.
- Design tokens.
- Testing utilities.

Create shared implementations only when there is genuine common ownership and a real maintenance benefit.

Avoid universal utility packages, excessive abstractions, cyclic dependencies, and tightly coupled applications.

Keep application-specific functionality independent where needed.

