# 17. CONTINUOUS AUTONOMOUS EXECUTION LOOP

Continuously execute:

**AUDIT → CLASSIFY → PRIORITIZE → SIMPLIFY → RESEARCH → DESIGN → IMPLEMENT REAL LOGIC → CONNECT DATA → WIRE FRONTEND → INTEGRATE → TEST → E2E VERIFY → FIX → DOCUMENT → RE-AUDIT → VERSION → RELEASE → VERIFY**

After every task:

1. Verify actual code.
2. Verify actual behavior.
3. Verify actual data flow.
4. Verify database persistence.
5. Check contracts.
6. Check consistency.
7. Check for duplicated functionality.
8. Update documentation.
9. Update project status.
10. Continue with the highest-priority remaining work.

Do not ask unnecessary confirmation for routine authorized work.

Do not stop after research.

Do not stop after creating a plan.

Do not stop after generating scaffolding.

Do not stop after implementing backend endpoints.

Do not stop after building frontend screens.

Do not stop after creating PRs.

Do not stop after a successful local build.

Continue until the three phases are genuinely complete and production has been verified, unless an actual external blocker prevents an authorized operation.

